The auth_jwt module validates JSON Web Tokens before nginx serves a
request.  The token is taken from the Authorization header or from a
cookie, its signature is checked against a configured key, and claims
such as the issuer or the expiry time are enforced.

Validated claims can be handed on to the backend as request headers, and
a failed check answers with an error or redirects to a login page.

This port only installs the module sources.  The module itself is built
by the nginx ports when their HTTP_AUTH_JWT option is enabled.
